horsepower (1.0.0-0ubuntu1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Live power from Intel and AMD RAPL energy counters, with a per-component
    breakdown (CPU, GPU, memory, storage, remainder) that omits any part the
    machine cannot measure.
  * Battery fallback for machines without RAPL.
  * Background service written in Rust: samples once a second, keeps a local
    SQLite log, activates over D-Bus and is started at boot.
  * Today, lifetime and cost totals, plus a per-minute chart of the last hour
    that leaves honest gaps while the machine sleeps.
  * Tariff and currency preferences, stored per user.

 -- HorsePower contributors <furkaniusprimes@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000
